WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.830
A castle at night.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.800
Inside, King Duncan is murdered.

3
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.600
Next morning, the sky stays
black: "by the clock ’tis day."

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.100
A falcon is brought down by an owl.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.010
The king's horses smash
out of their stalls.

6
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:19.020
And an old man whispers: "’Tis
said they eat each other."

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.540
One man dies.

8
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.400
So why does the whole of nature go wrong?

9
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.740
In this mission, you'll decode the
strange reports from the morning after.

10
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.120
You'll find out what
Shakespeare's first audience,

11
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.820
under King James, believed about kings.

12
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.160
And you'll compare the play's true
kings with the one it calls a tyrant.

13
00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:41.580
Your mission: explain why nature
breaks when a king is killed.
